Use two heaps: a max-heap for the lower half and a min-heap for the upper half. Keep them balanced (sizes differ by at most 1).

```cpp
priority_queue<int> lower;                            // max-heap
priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> upper; // min-heap

void addNum(int num) {
    lower.push(num);
    upper.push(lower.top()); lower.pop();  // balance
    if (upper.size() > lower.size()) {
        lower.push(upper.top()); upper.pop();
    }
}

double findMedian() {
    if (lower.size() > upper.size()) return lower.top();
    return (lower.top() + upper.top()) / 2.0;
}
```
